<title>CANADA: Alcan aims for 225,000-tonne smelter boost.</title>
<headline>Alcan aims for 225,000-tonne smelter boost.</headline>
<dateline>VANCOUVER 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alcan Aluminium Ltd will seek to expand its Kitimat aluminum smelter in the next decade by 225,000 tonnes a year at a cost of about C$1.2 billion, under a settlement deal with the British Columbia government.</p>
<p>The company and the government released the figures as part of the company's settlement announced today with the British Columbia government over Alcan's canceled Kemano hydroelectric project.</p>
<p>((Reuters Vancouver Bureau 604-664-7314))</p>
